FINDING (RED — the real vulnerability):
  verify_anchor returns root_verified ONLY — it does NOT check the
  signature. When the root is correct but the signature is invalid
  (random, wrong key, wrong format, missing, empty, null, 43-char
  base64url), verify_anchor returns success=True (the first tuple
  element) even though the message says "signature mismatch".

  This means: verify_anchor declares ROOT SUCCESS even when the
  signature FAILS. The message says rejection, but the boolean
  says acceptance. This is a critical API contract violation.

Type of failure: FALSE ACCEPTANCE (verify_anchor returns True
  despite signature failure — the boolean contradicts the message)

This satisfies the owner's criterion: at least 6 failure cases (7 RED).

